 "trace": {
  "model": "As classes/220/spec.json (same body and nose), bogies as in method.",
  "model.form.front": "The 220's measured front; the panel carried up round the screen to 3.52 m and the dark limited to the screen's surround (0.06 m round the glass): the old CrossCountry scheme paints the whole face yellow (pdo 221122, ppg 221135, 2025-26).",
  "liveries.XC": "The maroon and silver scheme the 221s still carry (pso 221113 2026-06, ppg 221135 2026-08, pdo 221122 2025-01): maroon cab end to door 1's front edge (pdo; raw #312632 overcast, drawn #3F3640), silver body (#C9CDD1, the lit upper side; raw #5D5E5F in shade), pink stripes beside each door (pdo), yellow face (raw #EBAE4B, drawn #F2B33F). The thin white X outline on the maroon is not drawn yet.",
  "liveries.GC": "Grand Central (221142-143; pgc1-3 2023-10, pgcx 2023-12): black (raw #3F4B54, no neutral; drawn #22272B), the orange band low on the bodyside (orange-gc #B6531C raw with a wide spread; drawn #D9621E), orange-yellow face (face-gc #D59510). Band heights read on pgc1 approximately (1.05-1.25 m).",
  "model.form.front.panelFoot": "The yellow's foot at the sides 1.40 (photo 1.32): at 1.32 its corners sat in the crease where the bumper's top lip meets the face and the decal clearance check read 0.15 mm off the body.",
  "model.form.front.couplerRecess": "The coupler recess between the two red bumper blocks (ptg levelled, 466 px/m: ±0.55 m, from the bottom to the yellow's notch at 1.55), black: the render showed a solid red nose there.",
  "liveries.XC.branding": "The red 'crosscountry X' on the nose's flank under the cab window, behind the lamp pod (pso 221113, 2026-06; 1280 px, close three-quarter): scaled along the flank by the cab side window's edges (1.58/2.42 m back, model) and up by its bottom and top (2.50/3.12): 0.32-1.61 m back, 1.22-1.42 m up (±0.15 m: the flank curves and the photo is close). Laid on the nose with the flank branding option; logos/XC.svg in its own red.",
  "model.form.front.pockets": "The coupler opening between the bumper blocks cut 0.3 m back (a void with the coupler in it), not painted black."
